Subject: [PATCH] first_boot: wait for initial_volumes_mounted before launching FirstBootPrompt

FirstBootPrompt's language list was empty on a genuinely fresh live
boot, even with 0029's get_available_languages() fix in place and the
compiled .catalog files confirmed present on disk (verified by
inspecting a running desktop session: 33 files under
/boot/system/data/locale/catalogs/x-vnd.Haiku-FirstBootPrompt/).

The cause is a race, not a missing catalog or a broken scan. data/
launch/user's top-level `run` block decides between the `first_boot`
and `desktop` targets unconditionally and immediately -- it has no
"on" gate. Every other thing that reads from the mounted system
packages (Tracker, Deskbar, LaunchBox, mail_daemon) is held behind
`on initial_volumes_mounted` in the `desktop` target; `first_boot`'s
job was the one exception, with nothing stopping it from starting
before mount_server's AutoMounter finishes activating the system
packages. On a live/CD boot, where everything is still being mounted
off the medium instead of already sitting on an installed disk,
FirstBootPrompt can win that race and call
BLocaleRoster::GetAvailableCatalogs() before the package that actually
provides those catalog files is active -- so the scan isn't wrong, it
is just looking at a directory that doesn't exist yet.

Add the same `on initial_volumes_mounted` gate the desktop target's
own services already use, so FirstBootPrompt starts after package
activation instead of racing it.

diff --git a/data/launch/user b/data/launch/user
index d15a4d19e3..39b28b872e 100644
--- a/data/launch/user
+++ b/data/launch/user
@@ -63,7 +63,9 @@ target desktop {
 }

 target first_boot {
-	job x-vnd.Haiku-FirstBootPrompt
+	job x-vnd.Haiku-FirstBootPrompt {
+		on initial_volumes_mounted
+	}
 }

 target installer {
